    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0946" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg886"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 1, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your dispatch of the 14th of September, No.
                    147, has been received. It contains a very full and careful account of the
                    devastations which were produced in the republic of Ecuador, by the terrible
                    earthquake of the 13th of August. Losing no time in giving publicity to the
                    painful narrative, I sincerely hope that it may excite not only the sympathies
                    but the active charity of all the civilized nations.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvin P. Hovey</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
